WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.408
Choosing a tracing tool.

2
00:00:01.688 --> 00:00:04.739
You need somewhere to send spans and a way to read them.

3
00:00:05.019 --> 00:00:17.456
The choice is less risky than it used to be, because the major LLM tracing tools accept OpenTelemetry data, so instrumentation you write against the OTel API isn’t locked to one of them.

4
00:00:17.736 --> 00:00:26.312
A few, described from their own documentation: Langfuse is an open-source platform you can self-host or use as a cloud service.

5
00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:37.024
Its data model is traces made of nested observations, plus scores for quality, and it runs evaluations, including LLM-as-judge, on production traces.

6
00:00:37.304 --> 00:00:38.584
It accepts OTLP.

7
00:00:38.864 --> 00:00:47.397
Arize Phoenix is an open-source observability and evaluation tool built on OpenTelemetry and the OpenInference instrumentation.

8
00:00:47.677 --> 00:00:57.256
It covers tracing, evaluations with LLM, code, or human graders, datasets and experiments for comparing versions, and prompt management.

9
00:00:57.536 --> 00:01:01.568
Arize also sells a separate managed platform (Arize AX).

10
00:01:01.848 --> 00:01:07.288
LangSmith, from LangChain, works with many frameworks and providers, not only LangChain.

11
00:01:07.568 --> 00:01:17.381
It offers dashboards and alerts, online evaluations, and annotation queues for human feedback, with cloud, hybrid, and self-hosted deployment options.

12
00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:19.027
Your existing backend.

13
00:01:19.307 --> 00:01:30.336
Anthropic’s docs list many general observability platforms (Datadog, Grafana Cloud, Honeycomb, New Relic, Sentry, and others) that accept these spans over OTLP.

14
00:01:30.616 --> 00:01:38.296
If your company already runs one, LLM spans next to your HTTP and database spans is a real advantage.

15
00:01:38.576 --> 00:01:41.883
Decide the way you’d decide on a model: with your own data.

16
00:01:42.163 --> 00:01:58.483
Send a week of real traces (with content policy settled first) to two candidates and check what matters to your team: can a reviewer read a full agent trace comfortably, can you filter by prompt version and join user feedback, where is the data stored and for how long,

17
00:01:58.763 --> 00:02:04.032
can you self-host if your privacy rules require it, and what does it cost at your span volume.
